      {
        "id": 140142,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-20T21:31:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Silverleaf, I know that it can be considered a \"kids\" movie, sorta, watch The Dark Crystal. It's pretty fantastic (obviously huge opinion there), but it's super dark and pushes the envolope of the \"puppets are for kids\" thing.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I saw it a while ago. Unfortunately my brain kept screaming THEY ARE PUPPETS AND THIS IS SUPPOSED TO BE SERIOUS at me and that's incredibly distracting I'm happy to give it another go though, but I think I'm irreparably broken.</p>",
